    {
      "id": "nRZ97kOuSGG6Z7kpzO9iK",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 303.24364338025885,
      "y": 160.63170676600328,
      "width": 1883.795654296875,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#eebefa",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bQ1",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1310644061,
      "version": 524,
      "versionNonce": 262038514,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1781513154016,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Google News is a digital service that aggregates and displays news articles from thousands of publishers worldwide in a scrollable interface for users to stay updated on current events.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Google News is a digital service that aggregates and displays news articles from thousands of publishers worldwide in a scrollable interface for users to stay updated on current events.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "3l3B22jVKTzOzRxzUcwts",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 335.1624697772131,
      "y": 1613.7965380308588,
      "width": 336.19598388671875,
      "height": 35,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bQ2",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 899908701,
      "version": 3400,
      "versionNonce": 1685358803,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1781516866144,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Key Concepts on the go ",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Key Concepts on the go ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "aoui3fXAGxZFf4vIU88Wf",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 319.14627689830763,
      "y": 1649.5582862982808,
      "width": 919.4992215988109,
      "height": 400,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#eebefa",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bQ4",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1744401587,
      "version": 1157,
      "versionNonce": 1626895699,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1781516874952,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1) What Are RSS Feeds?\n- Imagine every news website had a standardized notice board where they automatically post\na short summary every time they publish a new story. Instead of you visiting 10,000\nwebsites to check for news, each site keeps its own tidy list that any program can read.\n- That \"standardized notice board\" is called an RSS feed (RSS stands for Really Simple\nSyndication).\n- An RSS feed is just a special file (written in a format called XML) that lists recent articles.\nAn RSS feed is designed for computers to read — it's plain, structured, and predictable.\n\n2) Crawling and Polling\n- Polling = regularly re-checking each RSS feed (e.g., \"every 5 minutes, look for new items\").\nSimple and effective.\n- Crawling = a program that visits webpages and reads their content directly. Used when a\npublisher doesn't offer an RSS feed.\n- Be respectful: good crawlers obey robots.txt (a file where sites say what's allowed) and\ndon't hammer servers too fast. Learn more from Google's crawling documentation.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1) What Are RSS Feeds?\n- Imagine every news website had a standardized notice board where they automatically post a short summary every time they publish a new story. Instead of you visiting 10,000 websites to check for news, each site keeps its own tidy list that any program can read.\n- That \"standardized notice board\" is called an RSS feed (RSS stands for Really Simple Syndication).\n- An RSS feed is just a special file (written in a format called XML) that lists recent articles. An RSS feed is designed for computers to read — it's plain, structured, and predictable.\n\n2) Crawling and Polling\n- Polling = regularly re-checking each RSS feed (e.g., \"every 5 minutes, look for new items\"). Simple and effective.\n- Crawling = a program that visits webpages and reads their content directly. Used when a publisher doesn't offer an RSS feed.\n- Be respectful: good crawlers obey robots.txt (a file where sites say what's allowed) and don't hammer servers too fast. Learn more from Google's crawling documentation.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "2Or6gXU876BwqjoLWgqYw",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1289.8495621959264,
      "y": 284.27243844361305,
      "width": 916.2693684895834,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bQ5",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 249337693,
      "version": 10587,
      "versionNonce": 1548823613,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1781515862229,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Aggregated Feed → The ingestion pipeline (pollers → queue → parsers → database)\ncontinuously gathers articles from all publishers into one unified collection.\n- Infinite Scroll → We use keyset pagination (explained below) so each scroll loads the next\nbatch smoothly and efficiently.\n- Redirection → Each article stores the original source URL. When tapped, the app opens\nthat URL.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Aggregated Feed → The ingestion pipeline (pollers → queue → parsers → database) continuously gathers articles from all publishers into one unified collection.\n- Infinite Scroll → We use keyset pagination (explained below) so each scroll loads the next batch smoothly and efficiently.\n- Redirection → Each article stores the original source URL. When tapped, the app opens that URL.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
